# Story 7.1: the Containerfile's builder stage COPYs the full repo checkout
# (stations locate their repo root by marker-file walk-up, so a partial
# checkout breaks that) -- this file only strips VCS metadata, local caches,
# and build artifacts that are never needed inside the image.
#
# PATTERN SEMANTICS -- .dockerignore is NOT .gitignore. Docker matches each
# pattern against the whole context-relative path, so a bare `__pycache__/`
# matches ONLY a root-level one and silently misses all 67 nested under
# src/**. Anything that can occur at any depth therefore needs an explicit
# `**/` prefix. Entries WITHOUT one are root-anchored ON PURPOSE, and each
# such case was checked against `git ls-files` -- a root-anchored rule that
# guesses wrong ships the thing it meant to strip (`.idea/` did: this repo
# tracks `recipes/.idea/`, 10 files, which the root-anchored rule missed
# until it was widened below).
#
# TRACKED FILES ARE THE HAZARD, not untracked ones. A rule that swallows a
# git-tracked file makes the image quietly unlike the checkout, and nothing
# reports it -- the same failure class `.gitignore` hit on 2026-08-09, where
# a blanket `*.log` emptied `tests/fixtures/error_logs/` and turned the
# failure-analyzer's two unmatched-log cases into false greens. `.gitignore`
# fixed that with a narrow negation rather than by weakening `*.log`; the two
# negations below are the same fix, kept in step with it. Audit any new broad
# rule with: git ls-files | <match against this file>.

.git/

# The root `.pixi/` env is multi-GB and the builder stage materializes its
# own -- but `.pixi/config.toml` is GIT-TRACKED and load-bearing: it carries
# `run-post-link-scripts = "insecure"`, without which `pixi install` skips
# the post-link scripts that gdk-pixbuf (loaders.cache), gtk3, librsvg and
# graphviz all ship. Stripping it makes the image's install silently unlike
# every host install (verified: the host's pyforge-container env has
# `lib/gdk-pixbuf-2.0/2.10.0/loaders.cache`; a post-link-less install does
# not). `.pixi/*` rather than `.pixi/` so Docker drops each child wholesale
# instead of walking the whole env to honour the exception.
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml
# Nested pixi workspaces materialize their own envs (recipes/insightforge/
# and each src/shared/packages/* member declares its own manifest).
recipes/*/.pixi/
src/**/.pixi/

# BMAD Tier-3 runtime scratch -- gitignored, local-only, never git-tracked.
# `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts` is only a SYMLINK into the active
# project; the real per-project trees (run state, transcripts, patches,
# logs) live under projects/*/ and need their own pattern, or they ride
# along on any checkout where more than one station has run.
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/
_bmad-output/projects/*/implementation-artifacts
_bmad-output/projects/*/_root-fallback-fork-*

# bmad-loop run state -- a loop home is itself a full repo checkout (this
# story was developed in one), so `docker build .` from a loop home would
# otherwise ship every run's transcripts, patches and logs: 11GB in the
# steward home at the time of writing, and agent transcripts are exactly the
# kind of thing that carries a pasted credential. Mirrors .gitignore's four
# `.bmad-loop/*` entries with one root-anchored rule.
.bmad-loop/

# Build-host BMAD identity -- which project the marker/symlink point at is a
# property of the machine that built the image, not of the image. Baking it
# in makes two hosts produce two different images from one commit.
_bmad-output/planning-artifacts
_bmad/custom/.active-project
_bmad/config.user.toml
_bmad/_memory/

# Deprecated/historical content, not needed at runtime.
archive/

# Herald deck output -- large (84MB in this checkout) and not needed to run
# any station CLI. NOTE the real trade-off: herald's deck duty IS rooted
# here (`deck_pipeline.py`: `repo_root / "presentations" / slug`), so
# `herald deck` subcommands are host-only in this image by design. Story
# 7.4's volume mount is the seam if they ever need to run in-container.
presentations/

# Local secrets/credentials/state -- must never enter an image layer (these
# mirror entries .gitignore already treats as secret- or host-state-shaped:
# .env, .env.github, .secrets, .private, SDKs/). `.steward/` is the steward
# station's own repo-root state dir -- keys-inventory.yaml carries
# identity_path pointers, provenance and rotation history, budget.yaml the
# spend ceilings; neither belongs to whoever pulls the image. `/.herald/` is
# its exact analogue (AD-5's repo-local bridge/etag store, root-anchored in
# .gitignore for the same reason). `.claude/data/` is the gitignored mutable
# runtime cache (cf_atlas.db, vdb/, cve/, mapping caches) that Story 7.4
# mounts as a volume -- baking today's snapshot in would both leak whatever
# is locally cached and freeze stale state; `.claude/skills/data/` is its
# skill-scoped sibling.
.env
.env.github
.secrets
.private
SDKs/
.steward/
.herald/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/data/
.claude/skills/data/

# Python build/test artifacts -- all occur at any depth (each package under
# src/shared/packages/ grows its own), hence `**/`. Every tool listed here
# is installed by this workspace's pixi features, so every one of these can
# exist in a developer's checkout.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage
**/.venv/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/dist-conda/
**/build_artifacts/

# conda/rattler-build leavings -- this is a packaging factory, so a checkout
# that has run a local recipe build carries these (none are git-tracked).
conda-bld/
miniforge3/
**/*.conda
**/*.tar.bz2

# Node artifacts (present under some presentations/* subprojects)
**/node_modules/

# Editor/IDE metadata -- `**/` because `recipes/.idea/` is tracked too.
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/.junie/

# Misc local noise. The `*.log` negation mirrors .gitignore's: the
# failure-analyzer's fixture tree holds the repo's only tracked `.log`, and
# its absence turns two tests into false greens rather than failures.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
!.claude/skills/conda-forge-expert/tests/fixtures/error_logs/**/*.log
